> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1217700-recent-calls-for-gun-control-hows-it-effect-wod#post1217700\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">do you think Vamps would fear being affected that much? Or Black Eagle Mercenary company<br /> <br /> How about Pentex Think they's support or oppose this legislation...<br /> <br /> it could make things difficult for their first teams.</div> </div> </div> </div>I'm pro heavier regulations on thing IRL, that being said in the WOD I can imagine many of the &quot;progun&quot; arguments have a certain validity. Fewer guns is a good thing for vampires It makes feeding easier, it lets them kill with greater impunity etc.<br /> <br /> Similarly we already have situations where certain weapons require signficant liscencing that corporations put through the effort to engage in. Pentex wouldn't be effected. Those Kinfolk who stock up on guns to help fight off the formori when they come to push the Caern? those are the ones who get screwed there.<br /> <br /> Now I'll say again I only think these issues would exist because supernatural monsters, since there aren't really vampires and corporations aren't fighting against the warriors of Gaia I don't think at all these situations apply IRL.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T13:40:23-07:00","id":1217763,"title":"","content":"When it's harder to keep and bear arms, it's harder to use silver bullets as an effective defense against werewolves, so I'd expect vampires, Pentex, and anyone else who has a reason to fear werewolves would take that into consideration when they're deciding whether to support weapons bans. For the same reasons, werewolves will probably be most likely to support stricter gun restrictions.<br /> <br /> Any territory where handguns or firearms in general are banned, and any known &quot;gun free zone,&quot; is a place where all monsters will have less to fear from mortals.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/13713-wilson","name":"Wilson","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jul 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"182"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T13:46:21-07:00","id":1217766,"title":"","content":"keep in mind Kuei-jin and Hengoayoki DID survive japans extreme gun control.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T19:03:55-07:00","id":1217859,"title":"","content":"...and the World goes on without difference outside the US... <img src=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/images/smilies/biggrin.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" title=\"Big Grin\" smilieid=\"3\" class=\"inlineimg\" /><br /> <br /> <br /> Honestly, I think in the WoD, sups have their channels to get weapons, if they want. They re already working mostly under the radar of society. A lot of them doesn't really need guns anyway.<br />","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/>If nothing worked, then let's think!","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":4}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6363-pm\u00e1rk","name":"PM\u00e1rk","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6363_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Jun 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2363"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-11T20:32:25-07:00","id":1217876,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Wilson</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1217700-recent-calls-for-gun-control-hows-it-effect-wod?p=1217763#post1217763\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">When it's harder to keep and bear arms, it's harder to use silver bullets as an effective defense against werewolves, so I'd expect vampires, Pentex, and anyone else who has a reason to fear werewolves would take that into consideration when they're deciding whether to support weapons bans. For the same reasons, werewolves will probably be most likely to support stricter gun restrictions.</div> </div> </div> </div>Not really. The US isn't going to make it illegal for &quot;officially authorized&quot; types to have guns. What's far more likely to happen is it takes away the option for say a kinfolk to get a gun to help deal with Fomori. Pentex will have its first teams all legally able to have guns. And of course spree shootings will still keep happening because there are explicit supernatural beings who are making it happen.<br /> <br /> <div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Prince of the Night</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1217700-recent-calls-for-gun-control-hows-it-effect-wod?p=1217766#post1217766\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">keep in mind Kuei-jin and Hengoayoki DID survive japans extreme gun control.</div> </div> </div> </div>You can get guns in Japan. Japanese have a completely different situation than america. Since we are talking American issues since I don't think Gun control is a hot topic anywhere else.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-12T08:34:55-07:00","id":1217970,"title":"","content":"oh asked before?! How big a police problem do you think biting bullet's the Talen from Kinfolk: A breed apart, could cause?","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><a href=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" target=\"_blank\"><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imagizer.imageshack.us/a/img829/1897/8seg.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/2iw20supportergarou125p\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://imageshack.com/i/0j5hz8j\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /></a><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://imageshack.com/i/idnSdTJkj\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"https://i.imgsafe.org/97fd805379.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" />","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1153-prince-of-the-night","name":"Prince of the Night","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"4205"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-13T23:39:33-07:00","id":1218426,"title":"","content":"I think that gun control would impede low level characters - like most kinfolk, a lot of ghouls and maybe even some neonate vampires. Because they now don't have a way to get a gun. But your general mundanes have a harder time too.<br /> <br /> There will always be a black market for guns and those who will use it. Criminals and the Criminal minded; Those with ties to get permits through the layers of bureaucracy. - So Most Vampires will be able to do it themselves or trade boons to get it. They are generally more adept at blackmail and bribery, so getting legal versions or getting away with illegal arms is very likely. Especially if you know which Ventrue owns the Police Chief to get the charges dropped<br /> <br /> Werewolves are already Environmental-Terrorists, so I'm sure that they could get some weapons, but maybe more difficultly in general without a Glass walker hook-up, or looting them off some of their victims (Don't forget The First Share of the Kill for Greatest in Station) <br /> <br /> Mages? Can they - yes or no, maybe less coincidental to get your hands on one?","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T02:44:38-07:00","id":1218454,"title":"","content":"Making guns isn't well.. hard. I mean it is for your average person but for a society that exists completely off the books like all supernaturals do, having an underground gun shop is not going to be much more of a strain.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T17:16:23-07:00","id":1218737,"title":"","content":"That is another avenue - Having gunsmiths manufacture them.<br /> The time and cost would probably be higher for comparable weapons if they don't have mass production capabilities.<br /> <br /> The issue then, is the ammunition. getting a reliable source, even for the components if you have a bullet press.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/16927-illithid","name":"Illithid","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar16927_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Sep 2017"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1325"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-14T20:23:46-07:00","id":1218789,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Illithid</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1217700-recent-calls-for-gun-control-hows-it-effect-wod?p=1218737#post1218737\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">That is another avenue - Having gunsmiths manufacture them.<br /> The time and cost would probably be higher for comparable weapons if they don't have mass production capabilities.<br /> <br /> The issue then, is the ammunition. getting a reliable source, even for the components if you have a bullet press.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> yes and no? Your Camarilla city is going to have the infrastructure to hide something like this pretty easy. Your better Anarch and Sabbat cities might as well. Your more shithole cities are barely keeping things covered so they don't have time for elaborate hidden structures but that's its own thing. Similarly Glasswalker septs probably can pull this off, others on occasion but they might be more &quot;old fashioned&quot; type things like bowers and fletchers..<br /> <br /> Mages well if you can make a deathray a gun is pretty primtive technology.<br /> <br /> Changelings, same argument.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T00:57:37-07:00","id":1218821,"title":"","content":"It's also worth noting that making home-made guns is easier now than ever before.<br /> <br /> Machines like the <a href=\"https://www.wired.com/2015/06/i-made-an-untraceable-ar-15-ghost-gun/\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Gunner</a> allow any random person to create functional, untraceable firearms. They're designed in such a way that the machine itself does most of the work; the user is just required to move pieces around between steps.<br /> <br /> I suspect if gun control ever became a real problem, tech-savvy groups like the Glass Walkers, Clan Nosferatu, Virtual Adepts, and Society of Ether could use of such machines, or even design and sell their own. So long as customers can follow directions, they can produce their own arms. It's honestly never been easier to get one's hands on weapons, which is kind of scary.<br /> <br /> None of this, by the way, getting into the fact that you can also <a href=\"https://www.wired.com/2014/05/3d-printed-guns/\" target=\"_blank\">3D print functional firearms</a>. So there's that.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":6156,"user_link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","user":"Bluecho","date":". 05-15-2018, 04:00 AM"},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":1}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"3871"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T14:32:31-07:00","id":1219066,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Bluecho</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1217700-recent-calls-for-gun-control-hows-it-effect-wod?p=1218821#post1218821\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">It's also worth noting that making home-made guns is easier now than ever before.<br /> <br /> Machines like the <a href=\"https://www.wired.com/2015/06/i-made-an-untraceable-ar-15-ghost-gun/\" target=\"_blank\">Ghost Gunner</a> allow any random person to create functional, untraceable firearms. They're designed in such a way that the machine itself does most of the work; the user is just required to move pieces around between steps.<br /> <br /> I suspect if gun control ever became a real problem, tech-savvy groups like the Glass Walkers, Clan Nosferatu, Virtual Adepts, and Society of Ether could use of such machines, or even design and sell their own. So long as customers can follow directions, they can produce their own arms. It's honestly never been easier to get one's hands on weapons, which is kind of scary.<br /> <br /> None of this, by the way, getting into the fact that you can also <a href=\"https://www.wired.com/2014/05/3d-printed-guns/\" target=\"_blank\">3D print functional firearms</a>. So there's that.</div> </div> </div> </div><br /> <br /> Nos are another thing I'd point out. IF you can have a warrens you can easily have a machine shop capable of making guns.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/2715-lian","name":"Lian","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Apr 2014"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"5218"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2018-05-15T15:33:48-07:00","id":1219083,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>Lian</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/1217700-recent-calls-for-gun-control-hows-it-effect-wod?p=1219066#post1219066\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\">Nos are another thing I'd point out. IF you can have a warrens you can easily have a machine shop capable of making guns.</div> </div> </div> </div>Totally. Underground areas can muffle the sound of heavy machinery. There are plenty of tunnels through which the Nos can transport goods, keeping the police off the scent. And when you're an immortal who doesn't get out much, you have all the time in the world to learn how to operate such tools.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><div align=\"center\"><a href=\"http://archiveofourown.org/works/6956863/chapters/15862327\" target=\"_blank\">Magestuck: The Ascension</a></div>","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6156-bluecho","name":"Bluecho","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar6156_2.jpeg","title":"Member","rank":5,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key"